[],"v":[481,5702,13290,14064,18249,18311,21446]},"H1683":{"l":"דְּבּוֹרָה","x":"Dᵉbôwrâh","d":"Deborah, the name of two Hebrewesses","p":"deb-o-raw'","t":"deborah","g":"Deborah","fb":[["deborah","Deborah","Judge living before Israel's Monarchy","Prophetess and the one woman among Israel's judges. She sat under a palm tree between Ramah and Bethel and Israel came to her for judgment. Barak would not go against Sisera without her, so she went and told him a woman would get the credit, and Jael killed Sisera in her own tent.","person",9],["deborah-2","Deborah","Nurse living at the time of the Patriarchs","Rebekah's nurse, who went with her from Haran and stayed with the family for life. Genesis 35:8 records her death and burial under an oak below Bethel, which was named the oak of weeping.","person",1]],"v":[1019,6603,6604,6608,6609,6613,6624,6630,6635,6638]},"H1609":{"l":"גַּעְתָּם","x":"Gaʻtâm","d":"Gatam, an Edomite","p":"gah-tawm'","t":"gatam","g":"Gatam","fb":[["gatam","Gatam","Edomite living at the time of the Patriarchs","Esau's grandson through Eliphaz, and one of the chiefs of Edom, the dukes of the old translations, heading a clan and otherwise only a name in the lists.","person",3]],"v":[1051,1056,10288]},"H1681":{"l":"דִּבָּה","x":"dibbâh","d":"slander","p":"dib-baw'","t":"dibbah","g":"[the] whispering","fb":[],"v":[1085,4107,4144,4145,14343,16673,17122,19431,21361]},"H1605":{"l":"גָּעַר","x":"gâʻar","d":"to chide","p":"gaw-ar'","t":"gaar","g":"he rebuked","fb":[],"v":[1093,7165,14025,14929,15659,15918,17995,18731,19661,22687,22913,22913,23105,23130]},"H1612":{"l":"גֶּפֶן","x":"gephen","d":"a vine (as twining), especially the grape","p":"gheh'-fen","t":"gephen","g":"vine","fb":[],"v":[1181,1182,1484,3827,4316,5145,5790,5790,6766,6767,6898,8869,9642,10055,13235,15159,15205,15211,15638,16128,17566,17624,17634,17638,17804,17976,17977,18101,18270,18306,18345,18985,19074,19097,19165,20111,20755,20759,20830,20830,20831,20832,20890,22116,22225,22288,22297,22302,22332,22623,22784,22873,22921,22987,23130]},"H1657":{"l":"גֹּשֶׁן","x":"Gôshen","d":"Goshen, the residence of the Israelites in Egypt; also a place in Palestine","p":"go'-shen","t":"goshen","g":"of Goshen","fb":[["goshen","Goshen","","Joseph settled Jacob and the family here, in the eastern Nile delta, and Israel lived and multiplied there until the exodus. Pithom and Rameses were inside it, and it is generally identified with the Wadi Tumilat.","place",10],["goshen-2","Goshen","","Not the Goshen in Egypt but a stretch of Canaan's south that Joshua took, along with a town of the same name in the hill country.","place",3]],"v":[1368,1414,1414,1415,1420,1421,1424,1426,1447,1514,1732,1768,6105,6123,6253]},"H1647":{"l":"גֵּרְשֹׁם","x":"Gêrᵉshôm","d":"Gereshom, the name of four Israelites","p":"gay-resh-ome'","t":"gereshom","g":"of Gershon","fb":[["gershom","Gershom","","These verses are the census ones, Genesis 46:11, Exodus 6:16 and Numbers 3 and 4, where his family is counted and given its share of the tabernacle work. The note filed with them describes Moses's firstborn, born in Midian and named for a stranger there, who is a different man.","person",17]],"v":[1397,1671,1672,3709,3710,3713,3717,3765,3781,3784,3857,4005,4546,6387,6408,10455,10989]},"H1617":{"l":"גֵּרָא","x":"Gêrâʼ","d":"Gera, the name of six Israelites","p":"gay-raw'","t":"gera","g":"of Gera","fb":[["gera","Gera","Man living at the time of United Monarchy","He is only ever named as Shimei's father, and Shimei is the Benjamite who cursed David during Absalom's rebellion.","person",4],["gera-2","Gera","Man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness","The name ran in the Benjamite tribe. This Gera is in Genesis 46:21 and in 1 Chronicles 8:5, and Judges 3:15 makes a Gera the father of Ehud, the left-handed judge.","person",3],["gera-3","Gera","Man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness","One of 4 men called Gera. This one is a man from the wilderness years, named once in 1 Chronicles.","person",1],["gera-4","Gera","Man living before Israel's Monarchy","A man from the years before the monarchy, and 1 Chronicles is the only book that names him.","person",1]],"v":[1407,6583,8431,8527,8529,8778,10578,10580,10582]},"H1634":{"l":"גֶּרֶם","x":"gerem","d":"a bone (as the skeleton of the body); hence, self, i.e. (figuratively) very","p":"gheh'-rem","t":"gerem","g":"the bone","fb":[],"v":[1487,9769,13881,16894,17127]},"H1648":{"l":"גֵּרְשׁוֹן","x":"Gêrᵉshôwn","d":"Gereshon or Gereshom, an Israelite","p":"gay-resh-one'","t":"gereshon","g":"of Gershom","fb":[["gershon","Gershon","Levite living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness","Levi's eldest son. His descendants carried the tabernacle's coverings, curtains and hangings by cart through the wilderness. Exodus 2:22 and 18:3 carry the same name but belong to a different man.","person",14]],"v":[1576,2002,7023,10470,10471,10474,10497,10516,10525,10798,10998,10999,11101,12203]},"H1698":{"l":"דֶּבֶר","x":"deber","d":"a pestilence","p":"deh'-ber","t":"deber","g":"pestilence","fb":[],"v":[1635,1745,1757,3549,4120,5632,8705,8707,9022,10946,10948,11310,11337,11596,15162,15397,15400,19304,19445,19446,19448,19533,19603,19608,19625,19651,19652,19754,19766,19817,19896,19991,19996,20022,20557,20562,20573,20574,20591,20591,20695,20749,20751,21179,21306,21446,22279,22419,22772]},"H1639":{"l":"גָּרַע","x":"gâraʻ","d":"to scrape off; by implication, to shave, remove, lessen, withhold","p":"gaw-rah'","t":"gara","g":"it will be withdrawn","fb":[],"v":[1640,1643,1651,2087,3588,3972,4558,4882,4882,4883,5006,5272,13206,13210,13742,13762,17372,17961,19573,20116,20556,20788]},"H1610":{"l":"גַּף","x":"gaph","d":"the back; by extension the body or self","p":"gaf","t":"gaph","g":"body","fb":[],"v":[2080,2080,2081,16640]},"H1626":{"l":"גֵּרָה","x":"gêrâh","d":"a gerah or small weight (and coin)","p":"gay-raw'","t":"gerah","g":"gerah[s]","fb":[],"v":[2395,3595,3739,4273,21641]},"H1643":{"l":"גֶּרֶשׂ","x":"geres","d":"a kernel (collectively), i.e. grain",