ll country and won Caleb's daughter Achsah as his wife for it. Debir is also the name of a Canaanite king Joshua defeated.","place",8],["debir-2","Debir","King living before Israel's Monarchy","Joshua names him once, and he is a king from the years before the monarchy.","person",1]],"v":[6067,6102,6103,6128,6143,6209,6217,6217,6251,6396,6520,6520,10512]},"H1661":{"l":"גַּת","x":"Gath","d":"Gath, a Philistine city","p":"gath","t":"gath","g":"Gath","fb":[["gath","Gath","","Goliath's hometown, one of the five Philistine cities. The captured ark brought disaster on it, David later hid there with King Achish while running from Saul, and in the end David took it. Most identify it with Tell es-Safi, where a potsherd turned up carrying two names related to Goliath.","place",31]],"v":[6129,7327,7348,7366,7622,7641,7670,7782,7784,7932,7933,7934,7941,8042,8407,8600,8602,8809,8809,8810,8810,8811,9867,10556,10588,10891,10932,10934,11422,11738,14755,22451,22588]},"H1663":{"l":"גִּתִּי","x":"Gittîy","d":"a Gittite or inhabitant of Gath","p":"ghit-tee'","t":"gitti","g":"Gittite","fb":[["gittite","Gittite","Gath","A man from Gath. Obed-edom the Gittite kept the ark in his house before David brought it up to Jerusalem, and Ittai the Gittite brought his foreign troops to David's side when Absalom rebelled.","place",10]],"v":[6157,8167,8168,8407,8408,8411,8480,8599,10773,10931]},"H1650":{"l":"גְּשׁוּר","x":"Gᵉshûwr","d":"Geshur, a district of Syria","p":"ghesh-oor'","t":"geshur","g":"Geshur","fb":[["geshur","Geshur","","It was a small Aramean kingdom northeast of Galilee, and Absalom ran there after murdering his brother Amnon and stayed three years under his grandfather the king.","place",8]],"v":[6167,8084,8354,8355,8379,8388,8397,10329,10363]},"H1662":{"l":"גַּת־הַחֵפֶר","x":"Gath-ha-Chêpher","d":"Gath-Chepher, a place in Palestine","p":"gath-hah-khay'-fer","t":"gath-ha-chepher","g":"Gath","fb":[["gath-kephr","Gath-kephr","Gath-hepher","Jonah was born here, in Zebulun's territory, though the town is better known as Gath-hepher. Local tradition puts his tomb in the village of Mashhad by a hill called Nebi Yunus, near Nazareth.","place",2]],"v":[6334,6334,9921,9921]},"H1667":{"l":"גַּת־רִמּוֹן","x":"Gath-Rimmôwn","d":"Gath-Rimmon, a place in Palestine","p":"gath-rim-mone'","t":"gath-rimmon","g":"Gath","fb":[["gath-rimmon-d","Gath-rimmon","","In Dan's territory, and given to the Kohathite Levites. A second Gath-rimmon shows up in the Manasseh list, but 1 Chronicles 6:70 has Bileam there instead, which looks like a copying slip rather than two towns with one name.","place",3],["gath-rimmon-d-2","Gath-rimmon","Ibleam","Named once, in Joshua, and nowhere else.","place",1]],"v":[6366,6366,6405,6405,6406,6406,10523,10523]},"H1674":{"l":"דְּאָגָה","x":"dᵉʼâgâh","d":"anxiety","p":"deh-aw-gaw'","t":"deagah","g":"anxiety","fb":[],"v":[6450,16743,20149,20544,20697,20698]},"H1608":{"l":"גַּעַשׁ","x":"Gaʻash","d":"Gaash, a hill in Palestine","p":"ga'-ash","t":"gaash","g":"of Gaash","fb":[["gaash","Gaash","","Joshua was buried near this hill in Ephraim, close to Timnath-heres.","place",4]],"v":[6506,6554,8683,10705]},"H1640":{"l":"גָּרַף","x":"gâraph","d":"to bear off violently","p":"gaw-raf'","t":"garaph","g":"to bear off violently","fb":[],"v":[6644]},"H1660":{"l":"גַּת","x":"gath","d":"a wine-press (or vat for holding the grapes in pressing them)","p":"gath","t":"gath","g":"a winepress","fb":[],"v":[6665,12685,18867,20324,22355]},"H1603":{"l":"גַּעַל","x":"Gaʻal","d":"Gaal, an Israelite","p":"gah'-al","t":"gaal","g":"Gaal","fb":[["gaal","Gaal","Man living before Israel's Monarchy","He talked the people of Shechem into rising against Abimelech. When Abimelech brought his forces against the city, Gaal was beaten and driven out.","person",9]],"v":[6780,6782,6784,6785,6789,6790,6791,6793,6795]},"H1600":{"l":"גָּעָה","x":"gâʻâh","d":"to bellow (as cattle)","p":"gaw-aw'","t":"gaah","g":"lowing","fb":[],"v":[7343,12982]},"H1672":{"l":"דָּאַג","x":"dâʼag","d":"be 